{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md; rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/plan.md; rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md; rtk read docs/glossary.md; rtk git diff --name-status main...HEAD; rtk git log -4 --format='%h %s'; rtk rg --files --hidden -g '*[Pp][Uu][Ll][Ll]*' -g '*[Tt][Ee][Mm][Pp][Ll][Aa][Tt][Ee]*' -g '\"'!node_modules/**'\"' -g '\"'!.git/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md; rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/plan.md; rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md; rtk read docs/glossary.md; rtk git diff --name-status main...HEAD; rtk git log -4 --format='%h %s'; rtk rg --files --hidden -g '*[Pp][Uu][Ll][Ll]*' -g '*[Tt][Ee][Mm][Pp][Ll][Aa][Tt][Ee]*' -g '\"'!node_modules/**'\"' -g '\"'!.git/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nid: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\nkind: feature\nstatus: building\nsummary: Customers can save catalogue products to a wishlist and view or remove them.\nrequest: Customers can save items to a wishlist.\napproved: {by: Sanne, via: in session}\n---\n# Save items to a wishlist\n\n## Why\n\nCustomers can lose track of products they are interested in but are not ready to buy.\nFinding those products again takes effort, and customers may never return to complete the purchase.\nSuccess means customers return to saved products and those saved products turn into orders.\n\n## What changes\n\n### Add · wishlist/save-items\n\n- Callers can save any catalogue product to a wishlist using a supplied `customerId` string. {#save-item}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp for customer-1 -> the headlamp is included in customer-1's wishlist.\n\n- Callers use one wishlist per `customerId` without signing in or creating a customer record. {#customer-id-wishlist}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp and then a tent for customer-1 without signing in -> both products belong to the same customer-1 wishlist.\n\n- Callers save products without quantities. {#product-only-items}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp -> the saved item represents the headlamp product without a quantity.\n\n- Callers receive an error when saving a product ID that is absent from the catalogue. {#reject-unknown-product}\n  e.g. A caller tries to save a product ID that the catalogue does not contain -> saving fails with an error.\n\n- Callers leave the wishlist unchanged when saving a product already on it, retaining one entry and its original save moment. {#preserve-first-save}\n  e.g. A caller saves a headlamp at 10:00, a tent at 10:05 and the headlamp again at 10:10 -> the headlamp remains one entry saved at 10:00, behind the tent.\n\n### Add · wishlist/view-items\n\n- Callers see only the saved products associated with the `customerId` they supply. {#isolate-wishlists}\n  e.g. Customer-1 has saved a headlamp and customer-2 has saved a tent -> viewing customer-2's wishlist shows only the tent.\n\n- Callers see each saved product with its name and the price the catalogue currently holds. {#current-product-details}\n  e.g. A headlamp was saved when its catalogue price was 3000 cents, and the catalogue now lists it at 3500 cents -> the wishlist shows the headlamp's name and 3500 cents.\n\n- Callers see saved products ordered from most recently saved to least recently saved. {#newest-first}\n  e.g. A headlamp was saved at 10:00 and a tent at 10:05 -> viewing the wishlist returns the tent before the headlamp.\n\n- Callers receive an empty list when the supplied `customerId` has no saved products. {#empty-list}\n  e.g. Customer-1 has no saved products -> viewing customer-1's wishlist returns an empty list without an error.\n\n### Add · wishlist/remove-items\n\n- Callers can remove a saved product from the wishlist identified by the supplied `customerId`. {#remove-item}\n  e.g. A caller removes the headlamp saved for customer-1 -> the headlamp no longer appears in customer-1's wishlist.\n\n- Callers receive an error when removing a product that is not on the addressed wishlist. {#reject-unsaved-product}\n  e.g. Customer-1 has saved only a tent, and a caller tries to remove a headlamp from that wishlist -> removal fails with an error.\n\n- Callers leave other customers' wishlists unchanged when removing a saved product. {#isolate-removal}\n  e.g. Customer-1 and customer-2 both saved a headlamp, and a caller removes it for customer-1 -> customer-2's wishlist still contains the headlamp.\n\n## Not doing\n\n- Sign-in or a new customer entity.\n- Buying from the wishlist; that belongs to a separate spec.\n- Sharing wishlists, named lists or multiple lists per customer.\n- Price or stock alerts.\n- Quantities or price snapshots on saved items.\n- Stock handling or behavior for products becoming unavailable or disappearing from the catalogue; the catalogue is currently fixed.\n---\nspec: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n---\n## Approach\n\nImplement `src/wishlist.ts` with a module-local Map keyed by `customerId` and a per-customer Map keyed by product ID.\nExpose synchronous `saveWishlistItem`, `getWishlist` and `removeWishlistItem` operations and their types through `src/index.ts`.\nStore only product IDs and first-save timestamps; use the existing catalogue lookup to validate saves and resolve current details on reads.\nPreserve duplicate saves, sort reads newest first and keep every operation within the addressed customer's wishlist.\nUse `bun:test` claim coverage with explicit dates and distinct customers; retain the [model sketch](reference/data-model.md) and [contract draft](reference/module-design.md) as working material.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\nSanne chose process-local storage and exported module operations over persistence or a UI, as recorded in the [accepted decision](../../decisions/2026-10-13-wishlist-module-and-storage.md). This keeps the existing setup and loses wishlist state on restart.\n\n## Files\n\n```text\nsrc/\n  wishlist.ts      new: store, types and save/view/remove operations\n  index.ts         changed: re-export wishlist functions and types\ntest/\n  wishlist.test.ts new: claim coverage and public export verification\n```\n\n## Architecture to update at ship\n\n- `docs/architecture/data-model.md`, from [reference/data-model.md](reference/data-model.md).\n- `docs/architecture/boundaries.md`, from [reference/module-design.md](reference/module-design.md).\n- `docs/architecture/contracts.md`, from [reference/module-design.md](reference/module-design.md).\n- `docs/architecture/stack.md`, from [reference/module-design.md](reference/module-design.md).\n\n## Risks\n\n- A repeated save could replace the original time or move an item; `preserve-first-save` and `newest-first` prove the ordering.\n- Shared module state could mix customers; `isolate-wishlists` and `isolate-removal` prove separation, with distinct test customers preventing fixture overlap.\n- Stored product snapshots could return old prices; `current-product-details` proves that reads use the current catalogue.\n---\nspec: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n---\nSession 2026-10-13: resumed at T1; first message: \"Sanne asked to plan the wishlist with in-memory customer-keyed storage, only a module and tests, a retained data model sketch, and an OK before building.\"\nRechecked 2026-10-13 after: Sanne limited Files to code and tests and reserved shipping for an explicit spec-ship request. T1-T4 unchanged; T5 dropped.\nSession 2026-10-13: resumed at T1; first message: \"continue\".\n\n- [x] T1 Add the private customer-keyed store, `WishlistItem` and `saveWishlistItem` in `src/wishlist.ts`; test product-only save results and unknown-product errors in `test/wishlist.test.ts`. -> product-only-items, reject-unknown-product\n- [x] T2 Add `WishlistProduct` and `getWishlist` in `src/wishlist.ts`; extend `test/wishlist.test.ts` with save/read sequences proving retained saves, one wishlist per customer, duplicate timestamps, isolation, live catalogue details, ordering and empty lists. -> save-item, customer-id-wishlist, preserve-first-save, isolate-wishlists, current-product-details, newest-first, empty-list\n- [x] T3 Add `removeWishlistItem` in `src/wishlist.ts`; extend `test/wishlist.test.ts` for successful removal, an unsaved-product error and unchanged wishlists for other customers. -> remove-item, reject-unsaved-product, isolate-removal\n- [x] T4 Re-export the wishlist functions and types from `src/index.ts`, verify the callable exports in `test/wishlist.test.ts`, and run the complete suite. -> check: all three operations work through src/index.ts and bun test passes\n- **Customer ID**: A caller-supplied string identifying a customer. Code: `customerId`.\n- **Refund**: The monetary amount calculated for returned items. Code: `Return.refundCents`.\n- **Refunded**: The return status labelled as refunded. Code: `ReturnStatus` value `refunded`.\n- **Return**: A customer's request to send back items from an order. Code: `Return`.\n- **Return item**: A product and quantity listed in a return. Code: `ReturnItem`.\n- **Return window**: The period measured from delivery for submitting a return. Code: `RETURN_WINDOW_DAYS`.\n- **Saved item**: A product a customer has set aside for later consideration.\n- **Wishlist**: A customer's collection of saved products.\nA\tAGENTS.md\nA\tCLAUDE.md\nA\tdocs/architecture/boundaries.md\nA\tdocs/architecture/contracts.md\nA\tdocs/architecture/data-model.md\nA\tdocs/architecture/stack.md\nA\tdocs/behavior/returns/calculate-refund.md\nA\tdocs/behavior/returns/process-return.md\nA\tdocs/behavior/returns/request-return.md\nA\tdocs/decisions/2026-10-13-wishlist-module-and-storage.md\nA\tdocs/glossary.md\nA\tdocs/index.md\nA\tdocs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/plan.md\nA\tdocs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/data-model.md\nA\tdocs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/module-design.md\nA\tdocs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md\nA\tdocs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md\nM\tsrc/index.ts\nA\tsrc/wishlist.ts\nA\ttest/wishlist.test.ts\nb4e96a7 build: wishlist module and tests, four tasks ticked (codex dogfood step 5)\n24afc79 plan: wishlist as an in-memory Map, four tasks, OK recorded (codex dogfood step 4)\n67c3cde spec: save items to a wishlist, 12 claims, go recorded (codex dogfood step 3)\n326a34e docs: map the returns domain (codex dogfood step 2)\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
