{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/data-model.md; rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/reference/module-design.md; rtk read docs/architecture/data-model.md; rtk read docs/architecture/boundaries.md; rtk read docs/architecture/contracts.md; rtk git status --short; rtk git diff --check'","aggregated_output":"Purpose: retain the wishlist data model sketch as working material for implementation and the architecture update at ship.\n\n# Wishlist data model sketch\n\nThis is the proposed model for this spec, not a description of shipped code.\n\n| Value | Proposed fields or shape | Relations |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Module-local wishlist store | `Map<string, Map<string, WishlistItem>>` | The outer key is the supplied `customerId`; the inner key is `productId`, allowing one entry per product per customer. |\n| `WishlistItem` | `productId: string`, `savedAt: Date` | References a catalogue product by ID; stores its first save moment without quantity, name or price snapshots. |\n| `WishlistProduct` | `productId: string`, `name: string`, `priceCents: number`, `savedAt: Date` | A read projection combining a saved entry with current details from the existing catalogue in `src/products.ts`. |\n\n## Storage and reads\n\n- Create a customer's inner Map only after a catalogue product has been resolved successfully for the first save.\n- Copy the supplied save time on insertion. A repeated save returns the existing entry's values without changing its timestamp or position.\n- Resolve names and prices from the catalogue for each read, then order entries by descending `savedAt`. Equal timestamps retain insertion order.\n- Return fresh item values and copied dates so callers cannot mutate the stored entries through returned values or the supplied clock value.\n- Removing an entry addresses only the supplied customer's Map; an empty customer Map can be discarded.\n- An absent customer Map reads as an empty list. There is no separate customer record or wishlist ID.\n\n## Scope of the sketch\n\nThe spec leaves disappearing catalogue products and stock handling outside this change; this draft adds no behavior for those cases.\nCatalogue field access must use the existing exports and types when implementation begins; the catalogue itself is outside the change scope.\nKeep this file as working material after shipping; update `docs/architecture/data-model.md` from the implemented model instead of moving this draft there.\nPurpose: draft the wishlist contracts, module boundary and verification approach that inform implementation and architecture updates at ship.\n\n# Wishlist module draft\n\n## Public contracts\n\n| Export | Proposed contract | Result and errors |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `saveWishlistItem` | `(customerId: string, productId: string, now?: Date): WishlistItem` | Validate catalogue membership and save a product; default `now` to the current time. Return a copy of the new or existing saved entry. Throw `Error` for an unknown product. |\n| `getWishlist` | `(customerId: string): WishlistProduct[]` | Return the customer's saved products with current names and prices in newest-first order; return an empty list for a customer with no entries. |\n| `removeWishlistItem` | `(customerId: string, productId: string): void` | Remove the addressed customer's saved entry; throw `Error` if the entry is absent, including when that customer has no wishlist. |\n| `WishlistItem` | Exported TypeScript type | The stored product ID and first save time described in [the model sketch](data-model.md). |\n| `WishlistProduct` | Exported TypeScript type | The read projection described in [the model sketch](data-model.md). |\n\nCustomer IDs are used as supplied; do not add customer lookup, sign-in or normalization.\nThe draft does not promise exact error message text.\n\n## Module boundary\n\n- Implement the store, types and synchronous operations in `src/wishlist.ts`, using the existing catalogue lookup from `src/products.ts` and JavaScript built-ins.\n- Re-export the public functions and types through `src/index.ts` using that file's existing export convention.\n- Put the claim tests in `test/wishlist.test.ts`. The store remains private; tests use distinct customer IDs rather than adding a public reset API.\n- Use the existing TypeScript and Bun setup. No new packages, configuration, database, UI or changes to the catalogue module are planned.\n\n## Verification design\n\n- Name behavioral tests with full references such as `wishlist/save-items#save-item`; cover all 12 claims in the approved spec.\n- Use explicit dates for duplicate-save and ordering examples, without sleeps. Exercise save/read sequences to prove that successful saves actually remain in the customer's wishlist.\n- For `current-product-details`, arrange for a catalogue price to change between save and read using the existing catalogue test facilities, and restore any changed fixture or mock afterward. Do not add a production catalogue mutation API for this test.\n- Exercise two customers independently for reads and removal, including a failed removal from a customer without the saved product.\n- Verify the three functions through `src/index.ts` after adding the barrel exports, and run the complete `bun test` suite for regressions.\n\n## Architecture sources at ship\n\n- `docs/architecture/boundaries.md`: the Wishlist module, its source and test paths, catalogue dependency and public barrel.\n- `docs/architecture/contracts.md`: the implemented public contracts listed above.\n- `docs/architecture/stack.md`: the expanded TypeScript and Bun usage; retain the existing `bun test` command.\n\nKeep this draft as working material after shipping; architecture records the verified implementation.\n---\narea: data-model\n---\n# Data model\n\n| Entity | Key fields | Relations |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Return` | `id` (string, generated as `return-N` using a module-local counter), `orderId`, `items`, `refundCents` (number of cents), `status` (`requested`, `approved` or `refunded`), `requestedAt` (`Date`) | In-memory value defined in `src/returns.ts`; `orderId` references the supplied `Order.id`; embeds `ReturnItem[]` |\n| `ReturnItem` | `productId` (string), `quantity` (number) | Embedded in `Return.items`; product lookup uses the first matching `Order.lines` entry |\n| `Order` (returns input) | Returns reads `id`, `lines`, `discountPercent`, `status` and optional `deliveredAt` (`Date`) | Type defined in `src/orders.ts`; supplies `OrderLine[]` to the returns module |\n| `OrderLine` (returns input) | `productId`, `quantity`, `unitPriceCents` | Embedded in `Order.lines`; provides the recorded price and quantity for a matching `ReturnItem` |\n---\narea: boundaries\n---\n# Boundaries\n\n| Module | Path | Domain | May depend on |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Returns | `src/returns.ts` (re-exported by `src/index.ts`); tests in `test/returns.test.ts` | returns | `Order` from `src/orders.ts` through a type-only import; JavaScript built-ins for dates, arithmetic and collections |\n---\narea: contracts\n---\n# Contracts\n\n| Name | Kind | Input | Output | Consumers |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `calculateRefund` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `order: Order`, `items: ReturnItem[]` | Number of cents from `Math.round(subtotal * (1 - order.discountPercent / 100))`, where subtotal sums each entry's quantity times its first matching order line's unit price; throws `Error` for an unmatched product; performs no quantity or delivery validation | `submitReturn`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `submitReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `order: Order`, `items: ReturnItem[]`, optional `now: Date` (defaults to the current time) | New `Return` with copied item entries, the calculated amount and requested status; throws `Error` on validation failure; accepts supplied values without a return-history store | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `approveReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `ret: Return` | New top-level `Return` value with approved status; throws `Error` unless the input status is requested | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `refundReturn` | Exported synchronous TypeScript function in `src/returns.ts` | `ret: Return` | New top-level `Return` value with refunded status; throws `Error` unless the input status is approved; performs no payment-service call | `test/returns.test.ts`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n| `RETURN_WINDOW_DAYS` | Exported numeric constant in `src/returns.ts` | Read access | `30`, fixed in source; used with a day length of 86,400,000 milliseconds | `submitReturn`; re-exported by `src/index.ts` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
