{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"Marked the [spec](/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/scrubjay-example/.wt-codex/docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md) `shipped` locally and updated behavior and architecture docs. All 33 tests passed. Changes remain uncommitted.\n\n**PR title**\n\n```text\nfeature(customer-wishlist): Save items to a wishlist\n```\n\n**PR description**\n\n```markdown\n## Links\n- **Tracker:** None.\n- **Spec:** [Wishlist spec](docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md)\n\n## Description\nCustomers lose track of products they are interested in but are not ready to buy. Saving products helps them return later without searching again.\n\n- Callers can save any catalogue product using a supplied `customerId`.\n- Callers use one wishlist per `customerId` without signing in or creating a customer record.\n- Saved products have no quantities.\n- Saving a product absent from the catalogue returns an error.\n- Repeated saves preserve one entry and its original save moment.\n- Viewing a wishlist returns only products associated with the supplied `customerId`.\n- Saved products show their current catalogue name and price.\n- Saved products appear newest first.\n- Customers without saved products receive an empty list.\n- Callers can remove a saved product from the addressed wishlist.\n- Removing a product absent from that wishlist returns an error.\n- Removal leaves other customers’ wishlists unchanged.\n\nThe implementation exposes synchronous TypeScript module operations. Storage is process-local and resets on restart.\n\n## Unrelated changes\nNone.\n\n## Release impact\n**Release impact:** MINOR\n\n## Review\n- `bun test`: 33 passed, 0 failed across 4 files, before shipping documentation changed.\n- Fresh independent review found tests carrying references for all 12 claims, no claim contradictions, no correctness defects, and no outside-plan code.\n- Planned details without separate claims include insertion order for equal timestamps (tested), optional `now` with a current-time default, and defensive copies.\n- All 12 claims were copied verbatim into behavior documentation. All four planned architecture files were updated; both reference files remain unchanged.\n\n## Outcome\nSessions: 3, re-explained: 0. Grilling added viewing and removal, current catalogue details, duplicate-save preservation and customer isolation, while keeping sign-in, purchasing, sharing and alerts out.\n```"}}
